        "Content": "3 Castle Street, Macroom, Co. Cork P12VE81\n\nEnjoy the benefits of this deceptively spacious four-bedroom property, set just off the Square in the heart of Macroom Town. Positioned alongside the renowned Macroom Castle.\n\nBehind its traditional façade lies a home full of personality. Original fireplaces, elevated ceiling windows that bathe the kitchen in natural light, and spacious accommodation spread across four floors create a property with a truly distinctive feel. 3 Castle Street offers exceptional potential in its prime location. The property is in need of light refurbishment and suitable for an owner occupier or indeed would make an excellent investment property.\n\n\nLocation\n\nMacroom is a thriving market town nestled between Cork City and Killarney, renowned for its welcoming community, scenic riverside walks, and rich heritage. Residents enjoy immediate access to an excellent range of amenities including primary and secondary schools, cafés, restaurants, pubs, gyms, medical centres, and major retailers such as Dunnes Stores, Lidl, Aldi, and SuperValu. The nearby Macroom Castle Demesne and golf club provide beautiful outdoor spaces for recreation and relaxation.\n\nAccommodation\n\nGround Floor\nRecessed Hallway - quarry tiled floors radiator, glazed front door\nSitting Room Wooden floor, feature fireplace, radiator, alcove unit\nKitchen/Dinning Vinyl floor, fitted kitchen units, antique fireplace with stove, plumbed for washing machine and dishwasher, ceiling windows\n\n1st Floor\nBedroom 1 To front, Carpet, radiator, fitted shelving\nBathroom Wooden floor, whiteware, standing electric shower, radiator, shelving\n\n2nd Floor\nBedroom 2 - To front, carpet, radiator\nBedroom 3 - To rear, carpet, radiator \n\n3rd Floor\nBedroom 4 Carpet, radiator, fitted robes\n\nAdditional details\n\nGILA 126 sqm\nBER -E2\nBER Number - 118952704\nOil-fired central heating \nSolid fuel stove connected to radiators \nOpen fireplace\n\nDisclaimer: These particulars are issued by OM2 on the understanding that all negotiations are conducted through this office. While every care has been taken in preparing the particulars, they are for guidance only and do not form part of any contract. Descriptions, dimensions, distances, references to condition and permissions are given in good faith but are not to be relied upon as statements or representations of fact. Purchasers should satisfy themselves by inspection or otherwise as to the correctness of each statement. The vendor does not make or give, and neither OM2 nor any of its employees has authority to make or give, any representation or warranty in relation to the property."
